# SRG-APP-000368-AU-000240  -  CAT III
# The Central Log Server must be configured to generate reports that support
# after-the-fact investigations of security incidents.
#
# Generated from the benchmark and the assessment determinations, then kept
# by hand. Edit this file to change how this requirement is assessed here;
# it is read at run time. Regenerating refreshes the benchmark text in place
# and leaves the criteria, the determination and any verification block as
# they are.

id:              SRG-APP-000368-AU-000240
group:           V-206501
severity:        low
cat:             CAT III
determination:   APPLICABLE
grade:           C
decidable:       machine
confidence:      documented
cci:             CCI-001880
control_rev5:    AU-7

contribution:    Splunk can define a report whose dispatch range reaches back over past
                 events and can keep those events reachable by setting index retention and
                 an archive destination for buckets that roll to frozen, which is the
                 application's whole share of supporting an after-the-fact investigation.

governs:         indexes.conf - The indexes data is stored in, how large they may grow and how long data
                 is kept.
governs:         savedsearches.conf - Saved searches, scheduled reports and alerts.

check:           savedsearches.conf [<stanza name>] search non_empty
check:           savedsearches.conf [<stanza name>] dispatch.earliest_time non_empty
check:           indexes.conf [_audit] coldToFrozenDir non_empty
# --- vendor verification: generated, do not edit by hand
vendor:          indexes.conf [<index>] coldToFrozenDir https://help.splunk.com/en/splunk-enterprise/administer/admin-manual/10.4/configuration-file-reference/10.4.0-configuration-file-reference/indexes.conf
vendor:          indexes.conf [<index>] frozenTimePeriodInSecs https://help.splunk.com/en/splunk-enterprise/administer/manage-indexers-and-indexer-clusters/10.4/back-up-and-archive-your-indexes/set-a-retirement-and-archiving-policy
vendor:          savedsearches.conf [<stanza name>] dispatch.earliest_time https://help.splunk.com/en/splunk-enterprise/administer/admin-manual/10.4/configuration-file-reference/10.4.0-configuration-file-reference/savedsearches.conf
vendor:          savedsearches.conf [<stanza name>] dispatch.latest_time https://help.splunk.com/en/splunk-enterprise/administer/admin-manual/10.4/configuration-file-reference/10.4.0-configuration-file-reference/savedsearches.conf
vendor:          savedsearches.conf [<stanza name>] search https://help.splunk.com/en/splunk-enterprise/administer/admin-manual/10.4/configuration-file-reference/10.4.0-configuration-file-reference/savedsearches.conf
# --- end vendor verification

external:        The retention period, which sets how far back any investigation can reach,
                 is organization-defined and recorded in the site documentation.
external:        Capacity of the archive destination and the integrity of the media holding
                 it rest on the operating system and the storage platform.
external:        The investigative procedure that consumes the report, and the decision on
                 what period an incident requires, are organizational.
external:        The retention period itself, which is organization-defined: every index
                 declares frozenTimePeriodInSecs, so a test for the key cannot fail, and a
                 test on the value would report a finding against any site that chooses the
                 shipped six years deliberately.
external:        Preservation of frozen audit buckets by a script rather than a directory:
                 indexes.conf coldToFrozenScript is the documented equivalent of
                 coldToFrozenDir, and the two are alternatives, so an instance that uses
                 the script satisfies the objective by other means and the assessor reads
                 which of the two is set.

citation:        savedsearches.conf.spec:44 search, :564 dispatch.earliest_time, :571
                 dispatch.latest_time; indexes.conf.spec:382-388 [<index>] per-index
                 options, :684 frozenTimePeriodInSecs = <nonnegative integer> default
                 188697600, :713 coldToFrozenScript, :792 coldToFrozenDir.
finding:         Assessed at the application layer alone: no saved search defines a
                 retrospective report over the audit indexes in scope, or those indexes
                 state no retention period and no frozen archive destination, so records
                 age out by deletion and the application is not configured to the fullest
                 extent it can contribute to this requirement.
